<?xml version="1.0" standalone="yes"?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "docker.folders">
<!ENTITY author    "gcarstoiu">
<!ENTITY github    "&author;/&name;">
<!ENTITY launch    "Settings/DockerFolders">
<!ENTITY plugdir   "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY cfgdir    "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.10.27d">
<!ENTITY md5       "01d5bdcad5ac86152c3fe6518c7e4e19">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;"
        author="&author;"
        version="&version;"
        launch="&launch;"
        pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        icon="folder-open-o"
        min="7.2.0"
        support="https://github.com/&github;/issues">

<CHANGES>
###2026.10.27d
- The tip line at the foot of the table is replaced by the eight actions from
  the classic Docker view: Add Container, Start, Stop, Pause, Resume, Check
  for Updates, Update and (in the overflow) Container Size. The four
  lifecycle actions are one group labelled "All containers", and Stop and
  Pause confirm first - they act on every container on the server.
  Add Container uses Unraid's brand orange.
- Fix: searching for a folder icon showed broken images and never more than
  three results. It guessed filenames on both CDNs without checking they
  existed. It now searches each library's published index: "plex" returns 19
  real matches, and a name neither carries says so instead of showing
  broken tiles.
- Fix: on browsers with the URL bar at the bottom, a dialog's buttons were
  hidden behind it. Dialogs, menus and the progress panel now size to the
  visible viewport and keep clear of the home indicator.

###2026.10.27c
- Fix: on a phone the table jumped back to the left a second after being
  scrolled sideways. The live CPU/memory stream republishes about once a
  second and was redrawing the whole table each time; those figures are now
  written into the existing cells instead. Scroll position and the caret in
  the filter box also survive a background refresh.
- The table now reaches both screen edges on a phone instead of sitting
  inside a gutter, and the header stacks rather than crowding.

###2026.10.27b
- Fix: Unraid's own button styling repainted every control in the plugin -
  uppercase text, letter-spacing, a minimum width of 86px and an orange
  border - leaving switches, menus and icons as oversized orange boxes.
  The plugin now carries Unraid's "unapi" opt-out class, and its own element
  reset is both complete and specific enough to win on its own.
- The page no longer prints a second "Docker Folders" section header or
  repeats the "Containers" title. Unraid's heading is followed directly by
  the container counts.

###2026.10.27a
- Fix: the Docker page showed "Request failed (500)" and no containers.
  Unraid's DockerClient.php was being required from inside a function, which
  made the globals it declares ($dockerManPaths, $driver, $docroot) function
  locals, so every `global` lookup inside it resolved to null.
- Server errors now come back as JSON with the message and the failing file
  and line, instead of a blank 500, and are written to syslog (tag
  docker.folders).
- A stopped Docker service now says so, rather than rendering "0 containers".

###2026.10.27
- Initial release.
</CHANGES>

<!--
  Install the package.
-->
<FILE Name="&cfgdir;/&name;-&version;.txz" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
  <URL>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main/archive/&name;-&version;.txz</URL>
  <MD5>&md5;</MD5>
</FILE>

<!--
  Post-install: create the persistent config directory on the flash drive and
  drop any older package so the flash does not accumulate them.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
mkdir -p &cfgdir;/icons
[ -f &cfgdir;/folders.json ] || echo '{"version":1,"folders":[]}' &gt; &cfgdir;/folders.json
chmod 0644 &cfgdir;/folders.json

# keep only the package matching this version
for f in &cfgdir;/&name;-*.txz; do
  [ "$f" = "&cfgdir;/&name;-&version;.txz" ] || rm -f "$f"
done

echo "&version;" &gt; &cfgdir;/version

echo ""
echo "-----------------------------------------------------------"
echo " &name; &version; installed."
echo " Folders are stored in &cfgdir;/folders.json"
echo "-----------------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!--
  Uninstall. Folder definitions on the flash drive are kept on purpose so a
  reinstall restores them; remove &cfgdir; by hand to erase them.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
removepkg &name;-&version;
rm -rf &plugdir;
echo ""
echo " &name; removed. Folder definitions kept in &cfgdir;"
echo " Delete that directory to erase them."
echo ""
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
